### Variables globales
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7242
@adminToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
@userToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
@managerToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
@userId = user-123-456-789

### ========================================
### ACCESS RIGHTS TESTS (Admin)
### ========================================

### 1. Get all access rights (Admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 2. Get access right by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3. Create zone access right
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "zoneId": 1,
  "peripheriqueLogiqueId": null,
  "type": 1
}

### 4. Create device access right
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "zoneId": null,
  "peripheriqueLogiqueId": 1,
  "type": 2
}

### 5. Create full access right
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "zoneId": 2,
  "peripheriqueLogiqueId": 2,
  "type": 3
}

### 6. Update access right
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "zoneId": 1,
  "peripheriqueLogiqueId": 1,
  "type": 3
}

### 7. Delete access right
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights/3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8. Test unauthorized access (user trying to access admin endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 9. Test non-existent access right
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights/999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 10. Test create access right with invalid data
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/access-rights
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "",
  "type": 0
}

### ========================================
### USER ACCESS RIGHTS TESTS
### ========================================

### 11. Get user zone access rights
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/access-rights/zones
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 12. Get user device access rights
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/access-rights/peripheriques
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 13. Test unauthorized access to user access rights
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/access-rights/zones

### ========================================
### INCIDENT TICKETS TESTS
### ========================================

### 14. Create incident ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sujet": "Imprimante en panne",
  "description": "L'imprimante HP LaserJet ne répond plus et affiche un message d'erreur",
  "peripheriqueLogiqueId": 1,
  "zoneId": 1
}

### 15. Create ticket for zone issue
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sujet": "Problème de climatisation",
  "description": "La température dans la salle de réunion est trop élevée",
  "peripheriqueLogiqueId": null,
  "zoneId": 2
}

### 16. Create urgent ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sujet": "Panne électrique partielle",
  "description": "Plusieurs appareils ne fonctionnent plus dans le bureau principal",
  "peripheriqueLogiqueId": null,
  "zoneId": 1
}

### 17. Get ticket by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 18. Get tickets by status - Open
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/status/Ouvert
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 19. Get tickets by status - In Progress
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/status/En cours
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 20. Get tickets by status - Closed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/status/Fermé
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 21. Get tickets by user ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/user/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 22. Update ticket status to In Progress
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

"En cours"

### 23. Update ticket status to Resolved
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

"Résolu"

### 24. Update ticket status to Closed
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

"Fermé"

### 25. Assign ticket to another user (Manager/Admin only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/2/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

"manager-user-id-123"

### 26. Assign ticket to admin (Manager/Admin only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/2/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

"admin-user-id-456"

### 27. Delete ticket (Admin only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 28. Test unauthorized access to ticket creation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sujet": "Test sans auth",
  "description": "Test description"
}

### 29. Test get non-existent ticket
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/999
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 30. Test update non-existent ticket status
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/999/status
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

"En cours"

### 31. Test assign ticket without proper role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/1/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

"some-user-id"

### 32. Test delete ticket without admin role
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### 33. Test create ticket with invalid data
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/incidenttickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sujet": "",
  "description": ""
}